  "diagnosis_text": "**Diagnosis:** h1\u2192h5 traffic is being explicitly dropped at **s3**, where h1 attaches.\n\nEvidence:\n- `h1 \u2192 h5`: **0/3 replies (100% loss)**\n- h1\u2019s local connectivity works: `h1 \u2192 h2` **3/3 replies**\n- h5 itself and its local attachment work: `h5 \u2192 h6` **3/3 replies**\n- Other remote paths work: `h1 \u2192 h7` and `h3 \u2192 h5` both succeeded.\n- All currently used switches are available, and all configured inter-switch links are reported **ACTIVE**.\n\nThe s3 flow table contains this higher-priority rule:\n\n- Priority **50000**\n- Match: Ethernet source `00:00:00:00:00:01` (**h1**) and destination `00:00:00:00:00:05` (**h5**)\n- Action: **NOACTION** (drop)\n- Counter: **7 packets**\n\nThis rule overrides the normal baseline forwarding rule on s3 that would send traffic for h5 toward the network. Therefore the fault is not a physical link failure; it is an installed dataplane/policy drop rule on **s3**, specifically affecting frames from h1 to h5. Removal or correction of that rule is the required remediation.",
